   "forward": {
    "line": 32,
    "code": "def forward(self, x):\n    input_dtype = x.dtype\n\n    if self.qwen3_compatible:\n        x = x.to(torch.float32)\n\n    variance = x.pow(2).mean(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n    norm_x = x * torch.rsqrt(variance + self.eps)\n    norm_x = norm_x * self.scale\n\n    if self.shift is not None:\n        norm_x = norm_x + self.shift\n\n    return norm_x.to(input_dtype)\n"
   },
   "note": {
    "title": "RMSNorm",
    "text": "Divides each vector by its root-mean-square (with eps 1e-6) and applies a learned per-channel `scale`. Unlike LayerNorm it neither subtracts the mean nor adds a shift: one vector instead of two, and slightly less work. It computes in float32 whatever the input type."
   }
